  "aiContextParagraph": "The release of Belonging: A Journey of Love, the new memoir by former Congress president Sonia Gandhi, has prompted significant public and political discourse in India. The text covers personal experiences, including the assassination of family members and reflections on key moments in Indian history such as the 2002 Gujarat riots. Conversely, members of the Bharatiya Janata Party have utilized the memoir's release to challenge her historical narrative, particularly regarding her role as a perceived shadow authority during the United Progressive Alliance government. Specific criticisms from political rivals include her handling of the 1984 anti-Sikh massacres and the nature of her influence during the 1999 political developments. Amid the political scrutiny, the book has experienced strong commercial interest, and plans have been announced by Congress members to adapt her life story into a feature film.",
